HST PDF: the Start Center thumbnail of a PDF opened in HST PDF is drawn by PDFium, like the page.

Opening a PDF in HST PDF added it to "Recent documents" without a thumbnail. A new entry showed the
generic icon, and an entry that already had one kept it. Only an HST Draw open (Edit in HST Draw, the
option set to Draw, or a build before HST PDF) drew a page preview. That preview came from the Draw
import: with a build where the import dropped the /ca of a translucent watermark or signature line,
the line came out solid black. HST PDF then kept that preview on every later open, so the thumbnail
stayed dark while the opened file showed the line faint.

HST PDF now draws the thumbnail itself from the first page, with the PDFium renderer of its own
pages, at the size of other documents' thumbnails (512 px on the long side). The thumbnail matches
the opened file, and an old preview is replaced the next time the file is opened in HST PDF. A file
that needed a password gets the generic icon, as other encrypted documents do. With thumbnails
turned off (Common/History/RecentDocsThumbnail) or in headless mode the entry's thumbnail is left
unchanged, as for documents.

